{"chunk_id": "03af3e678c90", "text": "Bhishma recounts the moment he accepts Parashurama\u2019s challenge and rides to Kurukshetra for their fateful duel. After informing Satyavati and receiving blessings, Bhishma departs in a magnificent white chariot, ceremonially armed and accompanied by Brahmanical benedictions. At Kurukshetra, sages, gods, and ascetics gather to witness the extraordinary clash. Bhishma\u2019s divine mother Ganga appears and urges him to avoid fighting Parashurama, the legendary Brahmin warrior who once exterminated the Kshatriyas, but Bhishma refuses to withdraw. When the combat begins, Parashurama declares the Earth itself his chariot and the Vedas his steeds, symbolizing his spiritual power. Yet he also manifests a celestial chariot by will. Before fighting, Bhishma descends, reverently salutes his teacher, and asks for his blessing\u2014revealing the tension between duty, reverence, and warrior honor that defines this legendary encounter.\nBhishma and Parashurama meet at Kurukshetra for their fated duel despite Ganga\u2019s plea, exchange words of respect, and begin the battle.\nThemes: duty versus obedience, guru-disciple conflict, warrior honor, divine spectators, inevitability of battle", "vector": [0.010852552950382233, -0.024226807057857513, -0.024081576615571976, 0.013823142275214195, -0.012575495056807995, 0.020477261394262314, -0.022866936400532722, -0.0007174798520281911, -0.024979354813694954, -0.025507459416985512, 0.021216608583927155, 0.016173208132386208, -0.005901570897549391, 0.003531700698658824, 0.0025745106395334005, 0.0022510464768856764, 0.03831399977207184, 0.003317157970741391, 0.014918959699571133, -0.0076443166472017765, -0.0014374351594597101, -0.015130201354622841, 0.0021932851523160934, 0.02265569381415844, -0.03055085986852646, 0.02140144631266594, 0.025626283138990402, -0.011862553656101227, 0.0008565199095755816, -0.029758702963590622, -0.016793731600046158, 4.406890002428554e-05, -0.004304053727537394, -0.0075